  "scientific_conclusions": [
    "All35 sealed jobs,12 independent fixed-grid directional pairs, and4 saved response equations reproduce their reported values. This is provenance/calculation consistency, not an unconditional numerical-convergence certificate.",
    "Original negative selected mode1 curvatures of acid and calycosin are reproduced by frozen absolute-quadrature energy and gradient FD. Their moving/rebuilt grid counterparts were positive. The dominant mismatch is localized to fixed-vs-moving discrete quadrature second derivatives for those selected modes, rather than a demonstrated chemical saddle.",
    "The two drug CPHF physical-equation residuals are around1e-14 and their explicit H1 FockFD relative errors around1e-7. Ordinary CPHF solver inaccuracy is therefore a weak explanation for their .04–.05-scale original curvature discrepancy.",
    "Water stock-vs-wrapper inputs agree, but stock controls for both drugs are NOT_RUN and must not be generalized.",
    "Calycosin D1FD disagreement worsens when h shrinks from.005 to.001 (roughly17.25x). Saved SCF extra-cycle density changes are comparable to2h times the observed density-derivative error. This supports SCF-noise amplification as a testable explanation; it is not yet independently isolated."
  ],
  "paper_trust_requirements": [
    "Report fixed-grid vs rebuilt-grid semantics, exact grid levels/pruning, both h values, actual SCF orbital-gradient acceptance, energy/gradient response settings and all failed/not-run diagnostics.",
    "Do not report selected imaginary-frequency counts as chemically validated saddles, remove or flip frequencies by hand, or use a sum-rule-adjusted matrix as a corrected physical Hessian.",
    "Do not claim full minimum, complete corrected frequency spectrum, IR intensities, experimental band assignments, conformer ordering or solvent accuracy from these selected derivative checks.",
    "Use matching centers and identical settings for every finite-difference group; do not compare absolute energies across different quadrature grids as if they were one PES.",
    "For evidence of physically relevant local curvature, prioritize rebuilt-grid energy and full-grid-response gradient agreement across both grid densities and step sizes. Positive selected directions still do not establish all-direction positivity.",
    "Retain original raw Hessians and show numerical artifacts explicitly; manuscript language should separate converged derivative behavior for a chosen discretization from continuum molecular stability."
  ],
